        "You place the locked letter in the mailbox.",
        "The owner of the mailbox uses their private key to unlock and read the letter."
      ]
    },
    "receiving_a_letter": {
      "description": "The owner of the mailbox can also use their private key to sign a letter and put it in the mailbox. Anyone can use the public key to verify the signature and know it's from the owner.",
      "process": [
        "The owner locks a letter with their private key and puts it in the mailbox.",
        "Anyone can use the public key to unlock and verify the letter, knowing it's from the owner."
      ]
    },
    "security_benefits": {
      "description": "This system is secure because even if someone has the public key, they can't unlock the mailbox. Only the private key can do that. Similarly, only the owner can sign letters with their private key.",
      "key_points": [
        "Public key is like a mailbox lock that anyone can use to send a secure letter.",
        "Private key is like the secret key that only the owner has to unlock the mailbox and read the letters.",
        "This method ensures both confidentiality and authenticity of the messages."
      ]
    }
